    <dt>Slab model</dt><dd>Asymmetric four-layer c(4×4) Cu slab with eight atoms per layer, bottom two layers fixed, more than 28 Å vacuum, and a dipole correction normal to the surface.</dd>
    <dt>Electronic setup</dt><dd>PBE GGA, 380 eV cutoff, 0.1 eV Methfessel–Paxton smearing; exact code version and core-dataset identity are not reported.</dd>
    <dt>Ag hopping</dt><dd>4×4×1 mesh; finite-displacement frequencies use 0.04 Å steps; NEB uses eight intermediate images plus two endpoints.</dd>
    <dt>Cu mechanisms</dt><dd>Seven-image NEB calculations with a 2×2×1 mesh.</dd>
  </dl>
  <p>
    <strong>Not reported:</strong> exact force thresholds, spring constants, tangent/climbing-image settings, SCF controls, dataset provenance, or evidence that the mechanism catalog is complete. The source reports a conjugate-gradient relaxation but not enough detail to reproduce the path bit for bit. Modern execution and validation belong to the <a href="https://maxwell3919.github.io/DFT-Research-Workflow/">DFT Research Workflow</a>.
